  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), polled Monday 16 January 1928 in the Town Hall. Nine candidates were nominated for the five seats of the members retiring by rotation (John Hopps, Henry Megarry and others); seven went to the poll. Thirty-six papers were spoilt, some marked in the proportional-representation manner. Party labels are not printed. John Hopps: no party label printed in 1928. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Lurgan, 15 January 1925, listed as Unionist: Belfast weekly (BNA title 0004159), 10 January 1925, p. 11 (\"Municipal Elections ... Lurgan Members Elected\"); Lurgan, 15 January 1931, listed as Unionist: Lurgan Mail, 10 January 1931, p. 2 (local notes; and the editorial on \"the unopposed return of the five retiring members\")). William Waite: no party label printed in 1928. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Lurgan, Armagh County Council, 29 May 1930, printed 'U': Belfast News-Letter, 30 April 1930, p. 15 (\"Apathy in Rural Districts\"); withdrawals from the Lurgan Mail, 10 May 1930, p. 4 (\"No Contests in Armagh: County Council Nominees Withdraw\")). Edward Sullivan: no party label printed in 1928. At other elections he stood as Unionist (Lurgan, 15 January 1925, listed as Unionist: Belfast weekly (BNA title 0004159), 10 January 1925, p. 11 (\"Municipal Elections ... Lurgan Members Elected\"); Lurgan, 15 January 1931, listed as Unionist: Lurgan Mail, 10 January 1931, p. 2 (local notes; and the editorial on \"the unopposed return of the five retiring members\"))."
